  "question": {
    "text": "A plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> contains the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, and is perpendicular to the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Then which of the following points lies on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>?</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
